{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1480,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the distant future, aliens who live on\nasteroids near the center of the galaxy get"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5260,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in touch and want to come visit you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7380,
    "dDurationMs": 1220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so you tell them, “Of course!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8600,
    "dDurationMs": 1959,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I’m free any day this week.”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10559,
    "dDurationMs": 2861,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But they don’t know what that means - they\nlive in an asteroid belt and have a totally"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13420,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "different kind of calendar and, to them, the\nconcept of a “day” is very… alien."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17640,
    "dDurationMs": 3389,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you tell them that a day is how long it\ntakes for the Earth to complete a full rotation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21029,
    "dDurationMs": 1391,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about its axis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22420,
    "dDurationMs": 3689,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And as they input that into their computer\nsimulation, you notice a fatal flaw in your"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26109,
    "dDurationMs": 4551,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "explanation: as the earth rotates relative\nto the distant aliens, it moves a little bit"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30660,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "around the sun, and by the time it makes its\nway to the other side of the sun, our “daytime”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34770,
    "dDurationMs": 3719,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and “nighttime” have somehow switched,\nwith the sun directly overhead when one day"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38489,
    "dDurationMs": 3151,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "changes to the next, rather than in the middle\nof the day!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41640,
    "dDurationMs": 3239,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is not what we mean when we talk about\ncalendar days."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44879,
    "dDurationMs": 3471,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What you’ve actually described to the aliens\nis called a Stellar day and it’s measured"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48350,
    "dDurationMs": 5750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with respect to a distant, more or less stationary\nreference point far off in space - but our"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54100,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "concept of a day has more to do with the sun,\nnot the galactic center."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58120,
    "dDurationMs": 1209,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you try again."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59329,
    "dDurationMs": 4701,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This time you tell them that when Earthlings\nlook up at the sky, for each turn of the earth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64030,
    "dDurationMs": 2110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there’s a time when the sun is highest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66140,
    "dDurationMs": 3590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And you say that a day is the time it takes\nfor the Sun to get back to the highest point."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69730,
    "dDurationMs": 3740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so the Asteroid-ians tap away on their\ninstruments, calibrating them to your insightful"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73470,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "specifications until you notice that their\nday counter isn’t staying in sync with your"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77110,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "clock!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78110,
    "dDurationMs": 4230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s starting the new day earlier, and earlier\nand earlier each… day."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82340,
    "dDurationMs": 2450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then later, and later, and later."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84790,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This isn’t a bug in their programming - it’s\na feature… of the Earth’s orbit."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88890,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What you actually described to them is called\na Solar day, and it’s not the same thing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92460,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as a day kept by a clock."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94740,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Solar days use the sun as a reference point\nfor when “noon” is, but the length of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98490,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "time between when the sun is highest isn’t\nconstant - it changes up or down by a minute"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102970,
    "dDurationMs": 1250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "over the course of the year."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104220,
    "dDurationMs": 3370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This discrepancy is due to the complications\nof the earth’s orbit being elliptical and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107590,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the earth’s spin axis being tilted."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109630,
    "dDurationMs": 4590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If we used solar days in everyday life, we’d\neither need to have calendars and clocks that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114220,
    "dDurationMs": 4130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "changed the number of minutes and seconds\nin a day depending on the time of year, or"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118350,
    "dDurationMs": 3260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we’d need to have clocks that changed the\nlength of a second (or changed the number"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121610,
    "dDurationMs": 2420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of seconds in an hour) depending on the time\nof year."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124030,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And sundials kind of automatically do this!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126910,
    "dDurationMs": 1750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But they have other… drawbacks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128660,
    "dDurationMs": 4090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Anyway, changing the length of a second or\nthe number of seconds in an hour isn’t particularly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132750,
    "dDurationMs": 3140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "appealing for regular – or interplanetary\n– use."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135890,
    "dDurationMs": 4690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so you tell the asteroidaliens that a\nday is - more or less - an invented time period"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140580,
    "dDurationMs": 4379,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that is 24 hours long, where each hour is\n33 trillion oscillations of a special kind"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144959,
    "dDurationMs": 1750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "photon emitted by a cesium atom."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146709,
    "dDurationMs": 4030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if they want to know why a day is just\ndefined to be a fixed time period and how"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 150739,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that time period actually relates to the rotation\nof the earth, you can send them over to our"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154549,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "interactive video over on MinuteLabs."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156409,
    "dDurationMs": 4351,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It will guide anyone and everyone through\nthe details of solar, stellar, and standard"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160760,
    "dDurationMs": 4429,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "24 hour days; how they’re related; and how\nthe orbit of the earth affects them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 165189,
    "dDurationMs": 3211,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not only that, but it also lets you play around\nwith different orbits to see how it changes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168400,
    "dDurationMs": 1649,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the length of those days!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 170049,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The link is in the video description, or you\ncan just go to minutelabs.io and look for"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 173549,
    "dDurationMs": 1121,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the “What is a Day?”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174670,
    "dDurationMs": 4340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lab, and you’ll be fully prepared to coordinate\na visit with aliens… no matter what day"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179010,
    "dDurationMs": 580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that may be."
    } ]
  } ]
}
